{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JA9RMe7cjQ9pFzGBJhpsNH","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools\",\"number\":376,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(fix) O3-5993: Reports app shows literal {parameters} instead of the missing parameter names\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"jwnasambu\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-22T12:26:43.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-02T19:25:20.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-10-02T19:25:20.000Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/pull/376\",\"mergeCommit\":\"f462a28bf6f97d3a1c963e362b79c31b56f69bd4\",\"syncedAt\":\"2026-10-24T04:02:58.150Z\",\"tickets\":[{\"key\":\"O3-5993\",\"source\":\"ticket-pattern\"}],\"commits\":[{\"sha\":\"f462a28bf6f97d3a1c963e362b79c31b56f69bd4\",\"source\":\"merge-commit-sha\",\"verified\":true}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports-data-overview.component.test.tsx\",\"additions\":104,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports-data-overview.component.tsx\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1},{\"path\":\"packages/esm-reports-app/translations/en.json\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":1}],\"body\":\"\\r\\n\\r\\n## Requirements\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\\r\\n- [x] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\\r\\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n<!-- Please describe what problems your PR addresses. -->\\r\\nThe problem is that i18next interpolates placeholders with double braces ({{...}}), but the message used single braces ({parameters}), so the interpolation was never applied. This PR replaces {parameters} with {{parameters}} in the source string and all translation files, so the snackbar now lists the actual missing parameter labels e.g. \\\"Please provide the following parameters: Start Date, Location\\\". It also adds tests covering the missing-parameter snackbar behavior.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Screenshots\\r\\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Related Issue\\r\\nhttps://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5993\\r\\n\\r\\n## Other\\r\\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->\\r\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"kind\":\"issue_comment\",\"author\":\"greptile-apps\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-22T12:35:18.000Z\",\"state\":null,\"path\":null,\"line\":null,\"body\":\"<!-- greptile_summary -->\\n\\n<h2><a href=\\\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=67442325\\\"><picture><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\\\"><source media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\\\"><img alt=\\\"Retrigger\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\\\" align=\\\"right\\\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 4/5</h2>\\n\\nNot safe to merge until Chinese report validation messages include the missing parameter names.\\n\\n<h2>Findings</h2>\\n\\n1. <img alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\">&nbsp;**Keep Chinese parameter names** <a href=\\\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/pull/376#discussion_r4071645834\\\">▶</a>\\n\\n<h3>Summary</h3>\\n\\n\\n\\nThe report validation message now interpolates missing parameter names in the default translation, but the Chinese (`zh` and `zh_CN`) overrides still discard those names. This leaves Chinese-language users without the information needed to correct missing report inputs, so the change is not ready to merge.\\n\\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\\\"O3-5993: Reports app shows literal {para...\\\"](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commit/83130d5f6c3a4c1f143d3223761875bd6746a7e0)</sub>\"},{\"kind\":\"review_comment\",\"author\":\"greptile-apps\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-22T12:35:21.000Z\",\"state\":null,\"path\":\"packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports-data-overview.component.tsx\",\"line\":77,\"body\":\"<a href=\\\"#\\\"><img alt=\\\"P1\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\"></a> **Keep Chinese parameter names**\\n\\nThis call supplies the missing parameter labels, but the `zh` and `zh_CN` `missingParameters` translations override the fallback with `缺少参数` and omit `{{parameters}}`. Chinese-language users therefore see that parameters are missing without being told which inputs to provide. Update both translations to interpolate `{{parameters}}`; this must be corrected before merging.\\n\\n<details><summary><strong>Artifacts</strong></summary><br />\\n\\n**[Evidence from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/7995f6ba-876a-4463-8b42-62b50a04290e)**\\n\\n- The authored Node script loads PR-base and PR-head Chinese resources through i18next with the exact component interpolation options, proving that both localized outputs omit the supplied names.\\n\\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/58427868-1938-445c-9574-08fd6b59acda)**\\n\\n- Executed output records i18next 25.6.0 rendering \\\\`缺少参数\\\\` for zh and zh\\\\_CN before and after the PR despite receiving \\\\`Start Date, Location\\\\`, confirming the defect.\\n\\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/8127312a-2ec0-434d-b283-13bf52e30426)**\\n\\n- The captured PR diff shows the fallback change from \\\\`{parameters}\\\\` to \\\\`{{parameters}}\\\\` at the component while no Chinese resource change is present, isolating the remaining localization issue.\\n\\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/a10883ce-5b80-416d-8f1a-04ce80bc8c9b)**\\n\\n- The focused Vitest run passed all three report-overview tests, showing the existing English fallback behavior remains covered while the localized-resource issue is distinct.\\n\\n**[Chinese snackbar before PR #376 showing no parameter names](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/307dc3cc-6ba8-488b-bada-caefd3a35bb2)**\\n\\n- Chromium rendering of the PR-base zh snackbar shows only \\\\`缺少参数\\\\` whil\"},{\"kind\":\"review\",\"author\":\"greptile-apps\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-22T12:35:22.000Z\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"path\":null,\"line\":null,\"body\":\"\"},{\"kind\":\"issue_comment\",\"author\":\"greptile-apps\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-22T12:35:28.000Z\",\"state\":null,\"path\":null,\"line\":null,\"body\":\"<!-- greptile_outside_diff -->\\n\\n<h3>Comments Outside Diff</h3>\\n\\nThese findings sit on lines the diff does not cover, so they could not be posted inline. Each one leaves this list once its file changes.\\n\\n- <img alt=\\\"P2\\\" src=\\\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\\\" align=\\\"top\\\">&nbsp;**Chinese missing\\\\-parameters snackbar omits the parameter names** <a href=\\\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/pull/376\\\">▶</a>\\n\\n  - **Bug**\\n    - When a report has missing required parameters, the component passes the joined labels as `parameters` at `packages/esm-reports-app/src/components/reports-data-overview.component.tsx:77-79`. However, `zh.json:34` and `zh_CN.json:34` translate `missingParameters` as `缺少参数` without an interpolation token. i18next therefore renders only `缺少参数` rather than including labels such as `Start Date, Location`.\\n  - **Cause**\\n    - The PR corrects the default fallback interpolation syntax but the two Chinese localized overrides d